{
	"id": "sk-redis-session",
	"name": "SvelteKit Redis Session",
	"repo": "ethercorps/SK-Redis-SessionManager",
	"url": "https://github.com/ethercorps/SK-Redis-SessionManager",
	"summary": "A SvelteKit library that stores user sessions in Redis behind signed cookies, with one session store per Redis client: ioredis, node-redis and Upstash.",
	"description": "Shows the three session stores, the option interfaces they're built from, the shared cookie and signing helpers, and how an example app wires a store into its hooks.server handle.",
	"notes": "There's no shared base class or interface: the three stores are copy-paste siblings that share only redisSessionOptions and the shared.ts helpers. Store methods return an anonymous { data, error, message } literal, written here as Promise<object>. The @upstash/redis Redis class uses the shared.ts alias upstashRedisClient so it doesn't clash with ioredis Redis.",
